        "target_type": "Note",
        "author_id": 21826781,
        "target_title": "docs(auth): correct OAuth client ID requirements for the Git credential helper",
        "created_at": "2026-11-02T04:04:04.288Z",
        "note": {
          "id": 4137425417,
          "type": null,
          "body": "This is a focused documentation correction and I verified its technical claims against the code. I confirmed `oauthClientID`/`resolveClientID` in `internal/oauth2/config.go` indeed require a `client_id` on self-managed/Dedicated hosts but default it automatically on GitLab.com, matching the new doc wording. I verified the OAuth application is non-confidential (`printClientIDRegistrationInstructions` states \"Confidential: off\"), supporting the \"no client secret\" claim. I checked that interactive login already prompts for the credential helper via `credentialFlow.Prompt` unless `--setup-git-credential-helper` is set, confirming the new flag description and the \"Interactive sign-in offers this setup\" claim are accurate. I found no broken anchor links from the removed \"Recommended setup for OAuth-only instances\" section, and the `glab config set client_id ... --host ...` example matches the real command syntax. The change is low risk; only a minor wording nit is worth a second look.",
          "author": {
            "id": 21826781,
            "username": "GitLabDuo",
            "public_email": null,
            "name": "GitLab Duo",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/21826781/duo-bot.png?v=1792265836",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/GitLabDuo"
          },
